		)
	)
	(text_box "THE LM5164 IS A CONSTANT-ON-TIME REGULATOR -- IT NEEDS IN-PHASE RIPPLE AT FB TO BE STABLE\nCOT has no error amplifier. Datasheet 6.3.1 / table 6-1 require at least 20 mV of ripple at FB that is IN PHASE with the inductor\ncurrent. Ceramic output caps alone give capacitive ripple, 90 degrees out of phase; the classic failure is bursts of on-pulses followed\nby a long off-time. C9 / C15 are the type-2 feedforward caps the brief calls for -- they AC-couple output ripple to FB, but they do not\nby themselves make that ripple resistive. Finish it one of two ways before ordering boards.\n(a) TYPE 2, as drawn: add a small series resistance in the output-cap leg. Equation 4 gives RESR >= 20 mV / dIL, i.e. ~67 mohm (3.3 V\nrail, dIL 0.30 A) and ~54 mohm (5 V rail, dIL 0.37 A) at the 22 uH / 400 kHz operating point. Only ripple current flows in it (<1 mW)\nso it is nearly free, but it must be a real part -- do not rely on the cap's own ESR. (b) TYPE 3: the RA / CA / CB injection network of\nfigure 7-1 (453k / 3.3nF / 56pF in TI's 12 V design). That is what the EVM ships and it needs no series resistance at all.\nC9 / C15 = 100 pF is well above the equation-6 minimum (3.1 pF, 2.7 pF) and puts the coupling zero near 4.5 kHz, two decades below FSW,\nso the full output ripple reaches FB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 48.66 0)
		(size 103.19 18.28)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3e55743f-fe53-5503-a4b5-e6c70763c85b")
	)
	(text_box "WHERE EVERY VALUE CAME FROM\nU1 / U2 LM5164DDA, VREF = 1.200 V, RFB2 = 1.2 / (VOUT - 1.2) x RFB1 (eq 10): 348k/200k -> 3.288 V, 634k/200k -> 5.004 V, 6.0 uA each.\nTI recommends RFB1 in 100k..1M, so both sit inside the datasheet's own range. RRON: R4 20.5k -> 402 kHz, R7 31.6k -> 396 kHz; minimum\non-time at the worst case (VIN clamped to ~39 V by the input TVS) is 205 ns, well above the 50 ns floor. NOTE the LM5164 minimum VIN is\n6 V, so a deep crank dip drops both bucks out -- correct, but know it. C8 / C14 = 2.2 nF is MANDATORY and exact: the datasheet says a\nlarger bootstrap cap stresses the internal VCC regulator and damages the device. L4 / L5 = 22 uH gives 0.30 A (3.3 V) and 0.37 A (5 V)\nripple at 13.8 V in, 30-37% of the 1 A rating; pick a shielded part whose saturation current clears the LM5164's 1.5 A peak current\nlimit, not merely 1 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 68.44 0)
		(size 103.19 13.84)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4972193a-c7ac-5309-a666-316abe448d8e")
	)
	(text_box "PGOOD IS LEFT OPEN ON BOTH REGULATORS -- NOT AN OVERSIGHT\nPGOOD is open-drain and pulls LOW whenever its rail is down, which is precisely deep sleep. A pull-up would sink real current\ncontinuously while asleep (even 100k is 33 uA). No pull-up is fitted and no net is attached, so ERC reports these pins unconnected. No\nno-connect flags were added, on purpose: the ERC report is the reminder. If a rail-fault input is ever wanted, gate the pull-up -- do\nnot just add one.\nGND ON THIS SHEET IS BOARD GROUND. There is no GND_IN here; this sheet is downstream of the common-mode choke on power_input, so every\nground symbol is the board-side return. Star the converter grounds properly in layout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 83.78 0)
		(size 103.19 12.36)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "85ba4da4-7c46-5267-adcd-b4f50366a859")
	)
	(text_box "THE BUCKS RUN BELOW THE AM BAND ON PURPOSE: THE AM BROADCAST BAND IS 530 kHz - 1.7 MHz\nThis is a motorcycle and the battery harness is the antenna. The LM5164's maximum switching frequency is 1 MHz, which is INSIDE the AM\nband, so both bucks are placed BELOW it -- R4 = 20.5k gives 402 kHz on the 3.3 V rail, R7 = 31.6k gives 396 kHz on the 5 V rail\n(FSW[kHz] = VOUT[V] x 2500 / RRON[kohm]). Their fundamentals are clear of the band; harmonics 2 and 3 are not, and no LM5164 setting\ncan fix that. Mitigate in layout and filtering, not by raising the frequency: keep both buck power loops tiny, and remember the common-\nmode choke on power_input is there for this noise."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 36.28 0)
		(size 103.19 10.88)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "be387ae9-f881-58e6-a160-fe3bd1530abb")
	)
	(text_box "RAIL DOMAINS\nThree power domains plus one backup feed. +3V3_ALW is the always-on logic rail (U1, from VLOGIC_IN). +5V is the gated rail (U2, from\nVBAT) and is enabled only by EN_5V; with EN_5V floating, R19 holds the buck off. VBAT is the protected battery rail out of the input\neFuse. VBAT_B is the second protected feed (spec 4.3) and is not generated on this sheet. There is no boost converter and no switched\n3V3 rail on this board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 13 0)
		(size 103.19 9.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d4edd780-00b9-5c1d-b3a0-1665cd681bc8")
	)
	(text_box "SLEEP-BUDGET CRITICAL VALUES -- DO NOT \"TIDY\"\nBoth feedback dividers are >= 500 kohm on purpose. The LM5164's quoted quiescent\ncurrent does NOT include the external FB divider; a conventional 275 kohm divider\nwould add ~12 uA per rail, unbudgeted. At 348k/200k and 634k/200k each draws\n6.0 uA. A high-impedance FB node needs the feedforward cap for stability -- that\nis the trade being made deliberately."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 23.9 0)
		(size 103.19 10.88)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e0415660-5ace-594f-969b-fe49ffd0872e")
	)
